{"overview":"A young man in New York has exasperated his father because of his constant carousing and irresponsibility, so his father sends him to his uncle's ranch in the west. The young man arrives in the town of Piute Pass, which is being terrorized by Tiger Lip Tompkins and his gang, the Masked Angels. The Easterner befriends a young woman whose father is being held captive by Tompkins, and he decides to help her.","tagline":"A riot of rollicking fun!","cast":[{"n":"Harold Lloyd","c":"The Boy","p":"/alOOCzYnr08aEYekwsA3onrdeXk.jpg","q":"Q104340"},{"n":"Mildred Davis","c":"The Girl","p":"/ccRtJiD524ewwK0gFml47HYgnzp.jpg","q":"Q452630"},{"n":"Noah Young","c":"Tiger Lip Tompkins, The Bully, Leader of","p":"/g6JErSrooY8JZgUkADkFiBNGXiP.jpg","q":"Q3342510"},{"n":"James T. Kelley","c":"(uncredited)","p":"/rtZy3yPgkxNhb6PgdouGztL482A.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Sammy Brooks","c":"(uncredited)","p":"/v8Ltt1gF17LbihqIZwmGfXn0asQ.jpg","q":"Q3946526"},{"n":"Mark Jones","c":"(uncredited)","p":"/vCGVAoRLDRtMJL5yZ310PxF2y95.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Wally Howe","c":"(uncredited)","p":"/dCRkE4f9senVlBcCSGLT1Eubqcq.jpg","q":null},{"n":"J. Miller","c":"(uncredited)","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Belle Mitchell","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q4883660"},{"n":"Charles Stevenson","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q5082672"}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An_Eastern_Westerner","qid":"Q2211625","rel":{"US":{"d":"1920-05-02","c":"NR"}},"backdrops":["/69jI1TIsLsER8fUVqhw581qnMsm.jpg","/i8L9yW4BgDEXmp7znlahlbsCXLp.jpg","/xDltfDz5HSQuEzsfbgF5baMFPa3.jpg","/bwQyDEhjzWAxqBo1luVKXNQ4Ipb.jpg"]}